# {{title}}

## {{excerpt}}

![{{header-img-alt}}]({{header-img}})

The 19 [United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDG)]() are a central pillar of the .eco community. Everyone using a .eco domain needs to commit to one or more of the SDGs. That includes us as the [.eco registry](https://profiles.eco/bigroom/)!

However, we are not the only ones taking action. Across the domain name industry, there are many domain retailers (registrars) who are acting in support of the SDGs.

We’ve compiled those retailers who have pledged support for the SDGs. In some cases, the sustainability commitments are managed by a parent company; we’ve tried to clarify its connection with the brands you have heard of that they use to sell domain names. If there are retailers that we have missed that we should include, please <a href="#" class="chat-link">let us know</a>.


### GoDaddy

[GoDaddy](https://godaddy.com/) is the world’s biggest domain registrar. They publish an [annual sustainability report](https://aboutus.godaddy.net/investor-relations/esg/environmental-impact/) that outlines the actions that they are taking in support of the SDGs.

